 "note": [
  "Scripture is the Bíblia Livre (porbrbsl; ebible mirror por_bpm), pasted by script. Bounds quotes the KJV; where the Bíblia Livre differs in sense (Isa 26:4 Rocha eterna, Rev 3:16, Jas 5:16, Gen 32:26, Isa 64:7, Rom 15:31 desobedientes) the verse is kept and flagged. Two citations were re-sourced to the verse Bounds actually quotes (Deut 8:3 for “every word … out of the mouth of the Lord”, 2 Chr 34:21 for Josiah). 1 Pet 4:7 “watching unto prayer” is self_rendered because the Bíblia Livre reads “sóbrios”. The mirror’s Luke 7:50 carries stray machine-translation text after the verse; it was not copied.",
  "AI-translated (job #5234) in parallel chapters, then reconciled with Purpose in Prayer (same author) for one form per term: importunação, oração insistente, quarto de oração, homens de oração. Together with the shipped «Poder Através da Oração» and Purpose in Prayer this completes the pt plan praying-men, whose prose already exists. Awaiting native review."
